From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Antonio Sartori <antoniosartori@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 05:06:09 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 36/48] Make PermissionPromptDesktop::GetViewBoundsInScreen()
 pure virtual

PermissionPromptDesktop provided a default GetViewBoundsInScreen()
that returned std::nullopt. ExclusiveAccessPermissionPrompt relied on
it, so PermissionManager::GetExclusionAreaBoundsInScreen() did not
report any bounds for the modal keyboard/pointer lock prompt.

Remove the default implementation so that every subclass has to
provide one:
- ExclusiveAccessPermissionPrompt returns the web contents' container
  bounds while the prompt is showing, like EmbeddedPermissionPrompt.
- PermissionPromptQuietIcon explicitly returns std::nullopt, since it
  only shows an icon in the location bar.

Fixed: 536163128
Change-Id: Ic749eebe75e7d48523d3e2c5d044cea5c7b58e80
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8538367
Commit-Queue: Antonio Sartori <antoniosartori@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Judith Hemp <hempjudith@google.com>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1714368}
(cherry picked from commit 9d3a2a8f567c55a559ad0cab514d5a0c76e0c1fd)
